course: dictionary
lesson: 13434
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Honours is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. «The girl received honours for her bravery.» Here honours are awards and special praise, given for doing something brave.
explain: Honours can also be a verb. When it ends in s after he, she or it, it means shows respect or keeps a promise. «She always honours her word» means she always keeps her promise.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «She always keeps her word» still makes sense, so honours means keeps here. If the meaning fits the clues around the word, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Honours can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is often used in the plural: honours.
fact: As a noun, honours means awards, titles or special praise for great work or bravery.
fact: «With honours» means with extra praise for very good results, such as at school or university.
fact: «Do the honours» means do a special job, like cutting the cake or pouring the tea.
fact: In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, the King's Birthday Honours list people who are given special titles.
exercise: «The soldier received honours for his bravery.» What are honours here? | *Awards and special praise | Long, cold winters | Cakes and sweets | Soft, quiet voices
exercise: «He always honours his promise.» What does honours mean here? | Forgets | Breaks | Writes down | *Keeps
exercise: «Mia graduated with honours from university.» What does with honours mean? | *With extra praise for very good results | With a bag full of books | Late and tired | Without passing any tests
test: «Ben was asked to do the honours and cut the birthday cake.» What does do the honours mean? | *Do a special job for everyone | Hide the knife | Ask for help | Eat the first slice
test: «The mayor honours the old teacher every year.» Which word means the same as honours? | Forgets | Ignores | *Respects | Hides
exam: «The King's Birthday Honours list people who get special titles.» What do honours mean here? | Sad feelings | Meals for a big party | Long, slow walks | *Awards and titles
